+"""beta_overlay — M3: the BTC-beta overlay leg computed on the EXECUTED book (after POP -> RESHAPE -> CLAMP).
+
+Pre-registration: quant_research docs/PREREG_m3_beta_overlay_executed_book_2026-09-23.md (24c3f803f), §2 formula, §5 production.
+Why it is an executor-side leg and not a target-file weight: quant_research docs/RESULT_m2_btc_overlay_2026-09-23.md §1 — the
+executor re-demeans and re-scales every published target (anchor_loop RESHAPE_REDEMEAN = RESHAPE_RESCALE = True), so a BTC weight
+written into the file is spread back as -h/N over the whole book and the executed book stays dollar-neutral.
+
+THE FORMULA (prereg §2, zero free parameters; reproduced, not re-decided)
+    w_exec   = the executor's target AFTER POP -> RESHAPE -> CLAMP (USDT here; gross units = USDT / sizing gross)
+    beta_i   = the producer's per-name beta (target_live field `beta_overlay`, version VERSION): OLS slope with intercept of
+               the name's 4h log returns on BTCUSDT's over the most recent 180 4h bars completed at the anchor; >= 120 valid
+               pairs, else 1.0; clipped to [-1, 4]; BTCUSDT's own beta = 1.
+    beta_exec = sum_i w_exec,i * beta_i                   (USDT; the book's own BTC entry counts, with beta 1)
+    hedge     = -beta_exec                               (USDT) — the prereg's "-beta_exec x book gross notional" with beta_exec
+                                                          in gross units; the normaliser cancels, so no gross enters here.
+    target[BTCUSDT] = (the book's executed BTC entry, 0 if it was popped) + hedge — an INDEPENDENT leg: it is added AFTER the
+               reshape and never passes through it; the venue cap (clamp_venue_cap) still applies to the combined BTC target.
+    HOLD / DERISK / FLATTEN anchors never reach this code: a HOLD keeps the BTC position (hedge included) untouched.
+
+THE THREE MODES (config/book.json `beta_overlay.mode`; key or block absent == "off")
+    off     today's executor, byte for byte: nothing here is consulted beyond reading the mode (tests_beta_overlay [Z]).
+    shadow  the field is validated and the hedge that WOULD be placed is computed and recorded; the book, the orders and the
+            loop state are those of "off" (tests_beta_overlay [Z] runs shadow against the stripped executor as well).
+    on      the leg is placed.
+    Anything else (a typo, a non-string) is treated as "off" and paged HIGH — the overlay adds exposure, so an unreadable switch
+    must not add it; it also must not remove a book, which is why it does not block the anchor.
+
+BTC's ELIGIBILITY WHILE mode == on — the M3b rule (quant_research AMENDMENT_1, 912788743; evaluated by the M3b hook, c414ca4cf,
+reproduced here decision for decision so the evaluation describes production):
+    * The book stage (POP -> RESHAPE -> CLAMP) runs EXACTLY as in mode off, on the TRUE positions: every non-BTC name is bitwise
+      the off-mode book. BTC's book component is popped if it is dust and unheld, clamped if it is dust and held — as today.
+    * beta_exec is computed on that executed target (BTC's executed base value included, beta 1); leg = -beta_exec.
+    * BTC DUST-ONLY (it is untradable and `external_dust` — its PRE-reshape book target below min_notional_mult x minNotional — is
+      the ONLY recorded reason): the dust rule is re-applied to the COMBINED value C = BTC's executed base value + leg. C not
+      dust ⇒ target[BTC] = C and BTC is released from the clamp's lists (reduced / add_blocked / flatten_only / popped), so it
+      is not sent reduce-only ("applied_via_combined"); C still dust ⇒ nothing is touched ("combined_dust", the gap recorded).
+    * BTC TRADABLE ⇒ target[BTC] = its executed value + leg ("applied"); a combined value below the line is only recorded.
+    * EVERY OTHER untradability reason is a NAME-level fact the combined size cannot change ⇒ the leg is SUSPENDED for the
+      anchor: per-name stop (force_flat), stop cooldown, venue status / zero cap, venue meta, held-exit (BTC held while the
+      producer's file does not target it — 0 of the last 167 combo files did so), or an untradable BTC no source recorded
+      (fail-closed). BTC then follows the book's venue rules on its true position (reduce-only); first anchor HIGH, a
+      continuing suspension INFO with a number-free body (alarm_policy de-duplicates identical bodies).
+    * A leg of exactly 0 touches nothing.
+    * BTC is always in the priced symbol set (its mid is captured with the book's); with a zero producer weight and no position
+      it is dust-popped by the book stage exactly as an absent name would be, and then hedged via the combined value.
+    Two consequences of matching M3b, stated rather than hidden: an add_blocked BTC (its executed base value is its HELD
+    position, possible only when the book's BTC weight exceeds a near-zero hedge) combines the held position with the new leg;
+    and a producer file that drops BTC while the hedge is held suspends and unwinds the leg that anchor.
+
+MISSING IS NOT ZERO (prereg §5)
+    A missing field, a wrong version, a field for another anchor or cut-off, a malformed beta, or a name with a non-zero
+    executed target and no beta ⇒ NO hedge order this anchor and a HIGH page. The held BTC position is FROZEN (its target is
+    its current notional, delta 0) — never unwound as if the hedge were 0, never re-hedged as if every beta were 1.
+
+ACCOUNTING
+    anchors row `m3_beta_overlay` (this module's record); every orders row of BTCUSDT for that rebalance carries
+    `m3_overlay_leg` (the book / hedge / held split of the BTC target, read by binance_executor._order_row from the executor-level
+    record, never stamped on the plan dict); fills rows are unchanged (fills write contract) and join to the tagged orders rows on
+    (rebalance_id, symbol, order_type, attempt_idx). The chase experiment's neutrality basis and the end-of-anchor neutrality page
+    are judged EX-OVERLAY (the hedge's intended net is deliberate, not a tilt to be chased or paged).
+
+Pure functions only: no file, no network, no clock. anchor_loop owns the wiring (blocks marked `M3-BEGIN` / `M3-END`,
+single lines `# M3-LINE`, modified lines `# M3-ORIG:`; `strip_m3` removes them and must give back the pre-M3 source).
+"""
+from __future__ import annotations
+
+import hashlib
+import json
+import math
+from typing import Any, Dict, Iterable, List, Optional
+
+BTC = "BTCUSDT"
+FIELD = "beta_overlay"
+VERSION = "m3_beta_v1"
+CONFIG_KEY = "beta_overlay"
+MODES = ("off", "shadow", "on")
+# the frozen formula's parameters (prereg §2 / M2 m2_lib.py): the producer must declare exactly these
+N_WIN = 180
+N_MIN = 120
+CLIP_LO, CLIP_HI = -1.0, 4.0
+FALLBACK = 1.0
+H4 = 14400
+# untradable sources that do NOT stop the hedge: they are facts about the BOOK's BTC component (too small to trade, or not
+# targeted), and the hedge leg owns the position. Every other source — and an untradable BTC that no source recorded — is HARD.
+SOFT_SOURCES = ("external_dust",)       # the ONLY source the combined value can overrule (M3b "dust-only")
+# the executed hedge is compared with its intent at the TARGET level (exact arithmetic) and at the PLAN level (after lot
+# rounding). The plan-level tolerance is half a lot of BTC at the anchor mid, stated per anchor in the record.
+TARGET_DIAG_REL_TOL = 1e-9
+APPLIED = ("applied", "applied_via_combined")
+
+
+# ── config ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+def config(book: Optional[Dict[str, Any]]) -> Dict[str, Any]:
+    """{"mode": off|shadow|on, "error": str|None, "present": bool}. Pure. Absent key/block ⇒ off (today's behaviour)."""
+    if not isinstance(book, dict):
+        return {"mode": "off", "error": "book config unreadable", "present": False}
+    blk = book.get(CONFIG_KEY)
+    if blk is None:
+        return {"mode": "off", "error": None, "present": False}
+    if not isinstance(blk, dict):
+        return {"mode": "off", "error": f"{CONFIG_KEY} must be an object, got {type(blk).__name__}", "present": True}
+    mode = blk.get("mode", "off")
+    if not isinstance(mode, str) or mode not in MODES:
+        return {"mode": "off", "error": f"{CONFIG_KEY}.mode={mode!r} is not one of {MODES}", "present": True}
+    return {"mode": mode, "error": None, "present": True}
+
+
+# ── the field ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+def _finite(x) -> bool:
+    return isinstance(x, (int, float)) and not isinstance(x, bool) and math.isfinite(float(x))
+
+
+def betas_sha256(betas: Dict[str, float]) -> str:
+    """sha256 of the canonical JSON of the beta map (sorted keys, repr floats) — what the ledger records instead of 450 numbers."""
+    return hashlib.sha256(json.dumps({k: float(v) for k, v in sorted(betas.items())}, sort_keys=True,
+                                     separators=(",", ":")).encode()).hexdigest()
+
+
+def validate_field(raw: Any, anchor_ts: int, present: bool = True) -> Dict[str, Any]:
+    """Validate target_live's `beta_overlay` object for THIS anchor. Pure; never raises.
+    Returns {"ok", "reason", "detail", "betas", "n_obs", "version", "data_cutoff_ts", "n_betas", "n_fallback", "betas_sha256"}."""
+    def bad(reason, detail=""):
+        return {"ok": False, "reason": reason, "detail": str(detail)[:300], "betas": None}
+    if not present:
+        return bad("field_missing", f"target_live has no `{FIELD}` field (producer predates M3, or its beta step failed)")
+    if not isinstance(raw, dict):
+        return bad("field_malformed", f"`{FIELD}` is {type(raw).__name__}, not an object")
+    if raw.get("version") != VERSION:
+        return bad("version_mismatch", f"version={raw.get('version')!r}, expected {VERSION!r}")
+    try:
+        a = int(raw.get("anchor_ts"))
+        cut = int(raw.get("data_cutoff_ts"))
+    except (TypeError, ValueError):
+        return bad("field_malformed", f"anchor_ts / data_cutoff_ts not integers: {raw.get('anchor_ts')!r} / {raw.get('data_cutoff_ts')!r}")
+    if a != int(anchor_ts):
+        return bad("anchor_mismatch", f"field anchor_ts={a} != file anchor {int(anchor_ts)}")
+    if cut != int(anchor_ts):
+        # the formula's sample is the 180 bars COMPLETED AT the anchor: a cut-off before it is stale, after it is the future
+        return bad("cutoff_mismatch", f"data_cutoff_ts={cut} != anchor {int(anchor_ts)}")
+    decl = {"n_win": raw.get("n_win"), "n_min": raw.get("n_min"), "clip": raw.get("clip"), "fallback": raw.get("fallback"),
+            "btc": raw.get("btc")}
+    want = {"n_win": N_WIN, "n_min": N_MIN, "clip": [CLIP_LO, CLIP_HI], "fallback": FALLBACK, "btc": BTC}
+    if (decl["n_win"] != want["n_win"] or decl["n_min"] != want["n_min"] or decl["fallback"] != want["fallback"]
+            or decl["btc"] != want["btc"] or not isinstance(decl["clip"], list) or len(decl["clip"]) != 2
+            or [float(x) if _finite(x) else x for x in decl["clip"]] != want["clip"]):
+        return bad("params_mismatch", f"declared {decl} != prereg {want}")
+    betas, nobs = raw.get("betas"), raw.get("n_obs")
+    if not isinstance(betas, dict) or not betas:
+        return bad("bad_betas", "betas must be a non-empty object {symbol: beta}")
+    if not isinstance(nobs, dict) or set(nobs) != set(betas):
+        return bad("bad_betas", "n_obs must be an object with exactly the betas' names")
+    clean: Dict[str, float] = {}
+    n_fb = 0
+    for s, v in betas.items():
+        if not isinstance(s, str) or not s:
+            return bad("bad_betas", f"symbol key {s!r}")
+        if not _finite(v):
+            return bad("bad_betas", f"{s}: beta {v!r} not a finite number")
+        v = float(v)
+        if not (CLIP_LO <= v <= CLIP_HI):
+            return bad("bad_betas", f"{s}: beta {v} outside the clip [{CLIP_LO}, {CLIP_HI}]")
+        n = nobs.get(s)
+        if not (isinstance(n, int) and not isinstance(n, bool) and 0 <= n <= N_WIN):
+            return bad("bad_betas", f"{s}: n_obs {n!r} not an integer in [0, {N_WIN}]")
+        if s != BTC and n < N_MIN:
+            if v != FALLBACK:
+                # self-consistency of the producer: fewer than N_MIN valid pairs MUST be the fallback
+                return bad("bad_betas", f"{s}: n_obs {n} < {N_MIN} but beta {v} != fallback {FALLBACK}")
+            n_fb += 1
+        clean[s] = v
+    if clean.get(BTC) != 1.0:
+        return bad("btc_beta_not_one", f"beta[{BTC}]={clean.get(BTC)!r}, must be exactly 1.0")
+    return {"ok": True, "reason": None, "detail": "", "betas": clean, "n_obs": dict(nobs), "version": VERSION,
+            "data_cutoff_ts": cut, "n_betas": len(clean), "n_fallback": n_fb, "betas_sha256": betas_sha256(clean)}
+
+
+# ── the arithmetic ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+def beta_exec(target: Dict[str, float], betas: Dict[str, float]) -> Dict[str, Any]:
+    """beta_exec = sum_i target_i * beta_i (USDT) over every name with a NON-ZERO executed target. A name with a non-zero target
+    and no beta refuses the whole computation (never a default beta). Zero targets contribute 0 whatever their beta."""
+    tot, n, missing = 0.0, 0, []
+    for s in sorted(target):
+        w = float(target[s] or 0.0)
+        if w == 0.0:
+            continue
+        if s not in betas:
+            missing.append(s)
+            continue
+        tot += w * float(betas[s])
+        n += 1
+    if missing:
+        return {"ok": False, "reason": "beta_missing_for_targeted", "missing": missing, "n_missing": len(missing),
+                "beta_exec_usdt": None, "n_names": n}
+    return {"ok": True, "reason": None, "missing": [], "n_missing": 0, "beta_exec_usdt": tot, "n_names": n}
+
+
+def hard_block(untradable: Iterable[str], sources: Optional[Dict[str, Iterable[str]]]) -> List[str]:
+    """The NAME-level reasons BTC is untradable this anchor ([] = no name-level reason). Everything except `external_dust` is
+    name-level; an untradable BTC that NO source recorded is too (fail-closed)."""
+    if BTC not in set(untradable or ()):
+        return []
+    srcs = sorted(k for k, v in (sources or {}).items() if BTC in set(v or ()))
+    if not srcs:
+        return ["unrecorded_source"]
+    return [k for k in srcs if k not in SOFT_SOURCES]
+
+
+def dust_only(untradable: Iterable[str], sources: Optional[Dict[str, Iterable[str]]]) -> bool:
+    """BTC is untradable and `external_dust` is its ONLY recorded reason (the M3b condition for the combined judgement)."""
+    if BTC not in set(untradable or ()):
+        return False
+    srcs = {k for k, v in (sources or {}).items() if BTC in set(v or ())}
+    return srcs == {"external_dust"}
+
+
+def stage(mode: str, target: Dict[str, float], held_true: Dict[str, float], ext: Dict[str, Any],
+          sizing_gross: float, hard: List[str], prev_status: Optional[str] = None,
+          btc_floor: Optional[float] = None, dust_mult: Optional[float] = None, btc_dust_only: bool = False) -> Dict[str, Any]:
+    """The M3 stage, run on the target the book stage produced (the off-mode book). MUTATES `target` only when mode == "on".
+    `hard` = hard_block(...), `btc_dust_only` = dust_only(...), both taken BEFORE the book stage from the untradable sources;
+    `btc_floor` / `dust_mult` = BTC's venue minNotional and the book's min_notional_mult (the combined-value dust rule).
+    `prev_status` = the previous traded anchor's status (loop state): a suspension that CONTINUES pages HIGH once and INFO after.
+    Every status records the HEDGE GAP (`hedge_gap_usdt` = intended leg − placed leg at the target level; None when the intent
+    itself is not computable) and its reason — a leg not placed is never silent.
+    Returns {"record", "leg" ({BTC: ...} | None), "overlay_net_usdt", "alarms" [(sev, text)], "betas",
+    "release_btc" (the caller removes BTC from the clamp lists: the combined value overruled the book-component dust)}."""
+    held_btc = float((held_true or {}).get(BTC, 0.0) or 0.0)
+    b = float(target.get(BTC, 0.0) or 0.0)                  # BTC's EXECUTED base value (0 when popped; clamped value when held)
+    book_gross = float(sum(abs(float(v or 0.0)) for v in target.values()))
+    rec: Dict[str, Any] = {"mode": mode, "version_expected": VERSION, "btc_book_target_usdt": b, "btc_held_usdt": held_btc,
+                           "book_gross_usdt": book_gross, "sizing_gross_usdt": float(sizing_gross or 0.0),
+                           "hard_sources": list(hard or []), "btc_dust_only": bool(btc_dust_only), "overlay_net_usdt": None}
+    out: Dict[str, Any] = {"record": rec, "leg": None, "overlay_net_usdt": None, "alarms": [], "betas": None,
+                           "release_btc": False}
+
+    def _done():
+        rec["overlay_net_usdt"] = out["overlay_net_usdt"]
+        return out
+    v = validate_field(ext.get(FIELD), int(ext.get("anchor_ts") or 0), present=(FIELD in (ext or {})))
+    out["betas"] = v["betas"] if v["ok"] else None
+    rec.update({"field_ok": v["ok"], "field_reason": v["reason"], "field_detail": v.get("detail") or "",
+                "data_cutoff_ts": v.get("data_cutoff_ts"), "n_betas": v.get("n_betas"), "n_fallback": v.get("n_fallback"),
+                "betas_sha256": v.get("betas_sha256")})
+    be = beta_exec(target, v["betas"]) if v["ok"] else None
+    if be is not None:
+        rec.update({"beta_exec_usdt": be["beta_exec_usdt"], "n_targeted_names": be["n_names"],
+                    "n_beta_missing": be["n_missing"], "beta_missing_head": be["missing"][:12]})
+        if be["ok"]:
+            rec["beta_exec_gross_units"] = (be["beta_exec_usdt"] / sizing_gross) if sizing_gross else None
+            rec["beta_exec_over_book_gross"] = (be["beta_exec_usdt"] / book_gross) if book_gross else None
+            rec["hedge_intent_usdt"] = -be["beta_exec_usdt"]
+    usable = v["ok"] and be is not None and be["ok"]
+    reason = (v["reason"] if not v["ok"] else be["reason"] if not be["ok"] else None)
+    if hard:
+        rec.update(status="suspended_btc_untradable", reason="BTC untradable (name-level): " + ",".join(hard),
+                   hedge_gap_usdt=rec.get("hedge_intent_usdt"),
+                   hedge_gap_reason=("BTC untradable (" + ",".join(hard) + ")" if rec.get("hedge_intent_usdt") is not None
+                                     else "BTC untradable and the intent itself not computable: " + str(reason)))
+        if mode == "on" and prev_status == "suspended_btc_untradable":
+            # ★ a STABLE body (no numbers): alarm_policy de-duplicates identical bodies inside its window, so a 42-anchor
+            #   cooldown pages once per window instead of every anchor. The first anchor's HIGH (below) carries the numbers.
+            out["alarms"].append(("INFO", f"M3 对冲腿持续暂停: BTCUSDT 仍不可交易({', '.join(hard)}) — 首锚已页报; 对冲缺口逐锚记在 anchors 行; 原因解除后下一锚自动恢复。"))
+        elif mode == "on":
+            _gap = rec.get("hedge_intent_usdt")
+            out["alarms"].append(("HIGH", f"M3 对冲腿本锚暂停: BTCUSDT 不可交易({', '.join(hard)}) — 不下对冲单, 对冲缺口 "
+                                          f"{(format(_gap, '+,.0f')) if _gap is not None else '不可算'}U 记账; BTC 按书的场所规则处理"
+                                          f"(未持有 ⇒ 移出; 持有 ⇒ 只减/止损平仓, 现持 {held_btc:+,.0f}U)。"))
+        return _done()
+    if not usable:
+        rec.update(status="refused", reason=reason, hedge_gap_usdt=None,
+                   hedge_gap_reason="intent not computable (" + str(reason) + ") — the gap is UNKNOWN, not 0")
+        if mode == "on":
+            if held_btc != 0.0:
+                target[BTC] = held_btc                     # FROZEN: delta 0 ⇒ no BTC order; never unwound as if hedge were 0
+                rec["btc_frozen_at_usdt"] = held_btc
+                out["overlay_net_usdt"] = held_btc         # the frozen position is the (stale) leg's; not a book tilt
+            # BTC not held: there is no leg at all — the book's own BTC component (if any) is part of the neutral book
+            rec["btc_combined_target_usdt"] = float(target.get(BTC, 0.0) or 0.0)
+            _det = v.get("detail") if not v["ok"] else ("names without beta: " + ", ".join(be["missing"][:8]))
+            out["alarms"].append(("HIGH", f"M3 对冲腿缺失即不做: {reason} — {_det}。本锚不下对冲单; BTCUSDT 冻结在现持 "
+                                          f"{held_btc:+,.0f}U(不当 0 对冲平掉, 也不按 β=1 重算)。检查生产者 beta_overlay 字段。"))
+        else:
+            out["alarms"].append(("INFO", f"M3 shadow: 字段不可用 {reason} — 若开启则本锚不下对冲单"))
+        return _done()
+    hedge = -be["beta_exec_usdt"]
+    combined = b + hedge
+    thr = (float(dust_mult) * float(btc_floor)) if (btc_floor is not None and dust_mult is not None) else None
+    rec.update({"hedge_target_usdt": hedge, "btc_combined_target_usdt": combined, "combined_dust_threshold_usdt": thr})
+    if hedge == 0.0:
+        rec.update(status="zero_hedge", reason=None, hedge_gap_usdt=0.0, hedge_gap_reason=None)
+        return _done()                                     # a zero leg touches nothing (M3b order)
+    if btc_dust_only:
+        if thr is None:
+            rec.update(status="combined_dust", reason="combined dust NOT CHECKABLE (BTC minNotional / min_notional_mult unavailable)",
